      "text": "To simplify the expression \\((2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)\\), we first need to expand each of the products separately.\n\nStarting with \\((2x - 5)(x + 7)\\), we use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7 = 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 = 2x^2 + 9x - 35.\n\\]\n\nNext, we expand \\((x + 5)(2x - 1)\\):\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 = 2x^2 + 9x - 5.\n\\]\n\nNow we substitute these expanded forms back into the original expression:\n\\[\n(2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5).\n\\]\n\nWe then distribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses:\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5.\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine like terms. The \\(2x^2\\) terms cancel each other out, as do the \\(9x\\) terms:\n\\[\n2x^2 - 2x^2 + 9x - 9x - 35 + 5 = 0 + 0 - 30 = -30.\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form of the expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-30}.\n\\]",
